# Feature complete

`/feature complete` finishes the feature on `main`.

1. One commit on the feature branch. Reset `context/current-feature.md` in that same commit when the file exists.
2. The commit message has no `Co-authored-by` trailer. Read `git log -1` and strip a trailer before any push.
3. Check out `main` and fast-forward merge the feature branch.
4. Delete the local feature branch.
5. Push `main` when `origin` exists.
6. Delete the remote feature branch if it was pushed. After complete, `main` is the only branch.
7. Stop servers you started and close QA tabs.

If the work is already on `main` and there is no feature branch, commit and push `main`. Do not invent a branch to delete.
